Source: inspect-proxmox-host
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: UK AI Security Institute <153507562+art-dsit@users.noreply.github.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: https://github.com/UKGovernmentBEIS/inspect_proxmox_sandbox
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: inspect-proxmox-host
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         proxmox-ve,
         pve-qemu-kvm (>= 11.0.3-3+aisi1),
         libpve-network-perl (>= 1.6.7+aisi1),
         dnsmasq,
         iptables,
         jq
Description: Proxmox VE host configuration for Inspect sandbox evaluations
 Everything a Proxmox VE node needs beyond a stock install to host
 inspect_proxmox_sandbox evaluations: host-isolation firewall rules,
 link-local and IPv6 forwarding blocks, the optional guest egress lockdown,
 storage content types, and the .aisiN contract stamp on the reported
 version. Depends on the AISI rebuilds of pve-qemu-kvm and
 libpve-network-perl and pins them above upstream.

Package: inspect-proxmox-host-ec2
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         inspect-proxmox-host (= ${binary:Version}),
         curl,
         openssl
Description: EC2 boot-time fixups for AMI-launched Proxmox VE hosts
 Every launch from an AMI gets a new hostname, IP and instance-id. These
 units pin the node name, regenerate certificates and the root password,
 create the guest NAT bridge with the current management NIC, point the SDN
 dnsmasq instances at the VPC resolver, and ship pvestatd metrics to
 CloudWatch when the CloudWatch agent is installed.
